      "incorrect": "I live close the station.",
      "correct": "I live close to the station.",
      "note": "Use **close to** before a place; **near** needs no preposition."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "She is my near friend.",
      "correct": "She is my close friend.",
      "note": "For friends and family, use **close**, not **near**."
